/name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ADACHI IZUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURAHASHI AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO SEIICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ADACHI, IZUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURAHASHI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO, SEIICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The signal current (I1) output from the output terminal (11) of a semiconductor position detector (10) is converted to a signal voltage (V1) by a current-to-voltage converter (101), while the signal current (I2) output from the output terminal (12) of the semiconductor position detector (10) is converted to a signal voltage (V2) by a current-to-voltage converter (102). A comparator (200) compares signal voltages (V1, V2) and provides a maximum signal (Vmax) and a minimum signal (Vmin). An analog-to-digital converter (400) sets an analog-to-digital conversion range based on the maximum signal (Vmax) and outputs the minimum signal (Vmin) converted into a digital signal. Based on the comparison signal and the digital signal, a circuit (510) determines the position of incidence of light on the semiconductor position detector (10).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon cette invention, la sortie du courant (I1) du signal de la borne de sortie (11) d'un détecteur (10) de position à semi-conducteurs est convertie en une tension (V1) de signal par un convertisseur (101) de courant en tension, alors que la sortie du courant (I2) du signal de la borne de sortie (12) du détecteur (10) de position à semi-conducteurs est convertie en une tension (V2) de signal par un convertisseur (102) de courant en tension. Un comparateur (200) compare les tensions de signal (V1, V2) et génère un signal maximum (Vmax) et un signal minimum (Vmin). Un numériseur (400) établit une plage de conversion analogique-numérique sur la base du signal maximum (Vmax) et émet le signal minimum (Vmin) converti en un signal numérique. A partir du signal de comparaison et du signal numérique, un circuit (510) détermine l'incidence de la lumière sur le détecteur (10) de position à semi-conducteurs.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>